{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "No product behavior change. ci-python and validate select their runner through the CI_RUNNER_LABEL repo variable instead of a hardcoded label: unset, they resolve to ubuntu-latest and behave exactly as before, so forks of the public release export are untouched. Set to a runner label, the job routes to that runner instead.",
    "ci-python and validate cancel superseded PR runs (concurrency keyed on workflow+ref). cancel-in-progress is scoped to pull_request only, so a push run composing the evidence artifact a gate consumes is never cancelled -- only duplicate PR signal is.",
    "ci-python-full and the publish workflows are deliberately unchanged and stay on GitHub-hosted runners, so the authoritative interpreter matrix and anything that ships a release never depend on a local machine being awake."
  ],
